{"name":"Dog Rose","hex":"#e5c1d9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dog rose","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A European wild rose shrub of species Rosa canina, having fragrant white or pink flowers and stems with sharp spines.","A Rosa canina flower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dog_rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosa canina","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa canina, the dog rose, is a variable climbing, wild rose species native to Europe, northwest Africa, and western Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Divlja_ruza_cvijet_270508.jpg/330px-Divlja_ruza_cvijet_270508.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_canina"},{"title":"Dog","blocks":[{"text":"The dog is a domesticated descendant of wolves. Also called the domestic dog, it was selectively bred during the Late Pleistocene by hunter-gatherers. Dogs and the modern gray wolf share a common ancestor. Dogs were the first species to be domesticated over 14,000 years ago, before the development of agriculture, though genetic studies suggest the domestication process may have begun over 25,000 years ago. Due to their long association with humans, dogs have gained the ability to thrive on a starch-rich diet that would be inadequate for other canids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Huskiesatrest.jpg/330px-Huskiesatrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Aestivation.png/500px-Aestivation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Aestivation.png/500px-Aestivation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Quincuncial aestivation (A)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAestivation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Rosa_canina_244689792.jpg/500px-Rosa_canina_244689792.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Rosa_canina_244689792.jpg/1280px-Rosa_canina_244689792.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Rosa_canina_244689792.jpg/500px-Rosa_canina_244689792.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close-up of rose hips","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosa_canina_244689792.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Blo